  "raw_text": "108\n\nKli wih kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto make a return visit\n \n(on someone in the ministry) / hacer una revisita (a alguien en el\nministerio)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n):\n \nKli wih kaikma taim, naha sip sma daukaia: ...\n \nWhen you return to visit, you are able to do this: ...\n \n/ Cuando\nvuelva a visitar, podrá hacer esto: ...\n \n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-05/20\n):\n \nYawan nahki nu sa kristian waitna ai maritka wal ridi takan upla ra kli wih kaikaia dukiara?\n \n–\n \nHow do\nwe know that the Christian man prepared with his wife in order to visit again (make the return visit)?\n \n/ ¿Cómo sabemos\nque el cristiano se preparó con su esposa para volver a visitar (hacer la revisita)?)\n\nKli wih kaikanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nreturn visit\n \n/ revisita\n\n(Note/Nota: This refers to the visit itself and not the person we visit. The person who the return visit is made on is\ncalled:\n \nWih kaiki uplika\n \n/ Esto se refiere a la visita en sí y no a la persona que visitamos.\n \nLa persona a quien se\n\nhace la revisita se llama\n:\n \nWih kaiki uplika\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nKli wih kaikanka wala\n \n–\n \nnext return visit\n \n/ próxima revisita)\n\nKli wilwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cycle, to turn again, to spin again, to rotate again, to revolve again\n \n/ girar, girar de nuevo\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-05/20\n):\n \nPâsa ba nahki klin taki bara yawan ra kli wilwi tawisa ki?\n \n–\n \nHow is the breeze (air) becoming clean and\ncycling back (returning) to us?\n \n/ ¿Cómo se está limpiando la brisa (aire) y volviendo (regresando) a nosotros?))\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-05/20\n):\n \nNahki lî ba klin taki bara yawan ra kli wilwi tawisa ki?\n \n–\n \nHow is the water becoming clean and cycling\nback (returning) to us?\n \n/ ¿Cómo se está limpiando el agua y volviendo (regresando) a nosotros?)\n\nKli yapaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto go back to sleep, to sleep again\n \n/ volver a dormir, dormir de nuevo\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb37\n):\n \nKli yaps\n \n–\n \nGo back to sleep\n \n/ Vuelve a dormir)\n\nKli Smalkanka\n \n(\ndb\n;\n \nKli Smalkan\n-dba\n;\n \nLâ Kli Smalkan\n-bw\n;\n \nDeuteronomio\n-dbta\n)\n \n–\n \nDeuteronomy\n \n(Bible book) /\nDeuteronomio (libro bíblico)\n\nKlihtu\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nclam\n \n/ almeja\n\nKlik yabaia\n \n(\ntkl\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto click (with a mouse)\n \n/ hacer clic (con el mouse)\n\nKlin\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nclean\n \n/ limpio\n\nKlin bara pain\n \n(\njl26\n)\n \n–\n \nclean and good\n,\n \nwell-maintained\n \n/ limpio y bueno, bien mantenido\n\nKlin daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto make clean, to cause to be clean\n \n/ hacer limpio, hacer que sea limpio\n\nKlin kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be clean\n \n/ estar limpio\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-10/19\n):\n \nJehova wan mayunra lâka yamni kaikbia dukiara, yawan holikira kaia sa, wibia kaka, yawan klin kaia\nsa.\n \n–\n \nIn order for Jehovah to look at our worship as good (approve of our worship), we must be holy, that is to say, it must\nbe clean.\n \n/ Para que Jehová vea nuestra adoración como buena (apruebe nuestra adoración), debemos ser santos, es\ndecir, debe ser limpia.)\n\nKlin lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncleanliness, cleanness\n \n/ limpieza\n\nKlin munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto clean\n \n/ limpiar\n\nKlin takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become clean\n \n/ estar limpio\n\nUpla klin\n \n–\n \nclean person\n \n/ persona limpia\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nJehova\n \nupla klin nani ra latwan kaikisa\n \n–\n \nJehovah loves clean\n \npeople\n \n/ Jehová ama a las personas limpias\n)\n\nKlinsat\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nslingshot\n \n/ honda, hulera\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nPraukpraukia\n)\n\nKlipaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto blink, to wink\n \n/ parpadear\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-1Korint 15:51\n):\n \nwan nakra klipan kumi ra\n \n–\n \nin just one blink of our eyes\n \n/ en un abrir y cerrar de ojos )\n\nKlip daskaia\n \n(\ndict,dictu,dbta\n) (v-trans; intrans:\n \nKlip daswaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto put out a fire\n \n/ apagar un fuego\n\nDaskaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nDaswaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto put out, to extinguish, to turn off (as in a switch)\n \n/ apagar (como\nen un interruptor)\n\n(Note/Nota: Used on jw.org to turn off a feature / Se usa en jw.org para desactivar una función)\n\nKlip daswaia\n \n(\ndict,dictu,dbta,bh59\n) (v-intrans; trans:\n \nKlip daskaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto be extinguished\n \n/ estar extinguido\n\nCommonly used?\n\nDaswaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nDaskaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto go out, to be extinguished, to be extinct, to ease (pain)\n \n/ salir,\nextinguirse, aliviar (dolor)\n\n(Note/Nota: Verb irregularit\ny\n \n/\n \nI\nrregularidad\n \ndel verbo\n:\n \nDasbia\n \n(\nDaswbia\n)\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nAiseya\n \n42:3\n):\n \nLamp wíkka\n \ndaswaia kiasma taki ba sin, daskbia apia\n \n–\n \nThe lamp wick extinguished with\n\nsmoke happening (smoldering), will not put out\n)\n \n/ La mecha de la lámpara apagada con humo (humeante), no se\n\napagará)\n\nKlipas\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsandals\n \n/ sandalias\n \n(A\nlt:\n \nS\nandal suska\n)\n\nKlir\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nKler\n) (adj\n,\n \nadv)\n \n–\n \nclear, clearly\n \n/ claro\n, claramente\n\nKlir aisaia\n \n(\njl\n)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto speak clearly\n \n/ hablar con claridad",
